master prompt.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:29.649
And inside the Opus node sits the real
secret of this whole workflow:

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:33.369
our system prompt. This thing is built to
take any video apart

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.769
and reconstruct it as a perfect master
prompt,

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.209
it does not matter if it is a UGC ad,

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.128
a dance clip, or a product video.

00:05:40.129 --> 00:05:42.209
And this system prompt is exactly why

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:45.769
the results are this good, and it is
included in the free workflow.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.568
Opus never sees the original video,

00:05:47.569 --> 00:05:50.608
not even one single frame, Gemini
describes what happens,

00:05:50.609 --> 00:05:53.448
Opus writes the prompt, and that is why
the original woman

00:05:53.449 --> 00:05:55.167
cannot leak into our result.

00:05:55.169 --> 00:05:57.089
The prompt covers the recording format,

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.848
the setting, every action with its exact
timing,

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:03.369
and the complete audio, and it never
invents cuts or camera moves

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:05.288
that the analysis did not prove.

00:06:05.289 --> 00:06:07.608
Then everything goes into the Seedance
node,

00:06:07.609 --> 00:06:10.848
the master prompt, Lina's three
references, and nothing else,

00:06:10.849 --> 00:06:14.283
we set 720p, thirty seconds, and hit
generate.

00:06:14.289 --> 00:06:16.328
And real quick, because this is important:

00:06:16.329 --> 00:06:18.209
